            <h1>Innovating Kenyan Real Estate: Meet Eliya Sande, Founder of QejaConnect</h1>
            <div class="meta">Published by QejaConnect Team &bull; Founder Spotlight</div>

            <img src="https://eliyasande65-lang.github.io/eliya/images/img1.jpg" alt="Eliya Sande (Elias Sande), Founder of QejaConnect" class="hero-image">

            <p>The Kenyan real estate landscape is undergoing a digital transformation, and at the forefront of this movement is <strong>Eliya Sande</strong>—also widely recognized by his community and peers as <strong>Elias Sande</strong>. As the visionary founder of <strong>QejaConnect</strong>, Eliya has dedicated his entrepreneurial journey to solving one of the most persistent challenges in the urban housing market: bridging the gap between property owners and home seekers.</p>

            <h2>The Vision Behind QejaConnect</h2>
            <p>Finding a reliable tenant or a decent house in Kenya's fast-growing urban centers has traditionally been fraught with inefficiencies, untrustworthy brokers, and endless physical searches. Recognizing this friction, Eliya Sande conceptualized QejaConnect as a seamless, transparent digital solution.</p>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <p>QejaConnect is a premier platform engineered to directly connect verified landlords with potential tenants in Kenya, cutting out unnecessary intermediaries and building a trusted rental ecosystem.</p>
            </div>

            <h2>Leadership and Impact</h2>
            <p>Under the leadership of Elias Sande, QejaConnect focuses on user-centric design, reliability, and security. By leveraging modern technology, the platform empowers property owners to manage vacancies effortlessly while granting everyday Kenyans transparent access to housing options that fit their needs and budgets.</p>

            <p>Eliya’s commitment to tech-driven social impact continues to shape the future of proptech in Kenya, positioning QejaConnect as an essential tool for modern property management and apartment hunting.</p>
